6,4 contratos. La razón entre observados y esperados es 4,7, con un intervalo de confianza del 95 % de 2,8 a 8,0. En diciembre se adjudicó el 3 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 8 % de todos sus contratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 24 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.092 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La concentración de contratos al límite no indica malas prácticas. Puede deberse a variaciones de precios o necesidades específicas. No refleja actos ilícitos ni errores.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos al límite se reparten entre varios proveedores. Verificar si el mismo adjudicatario repite contratos en distintas fechas. Analizar si los contratos se agrupan para cubrir necesidades específicas.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 30 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 6.4 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 4.7, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.8 to 8.0. Contract [1], for 14,092 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: a pile-up of amounts just under the limit is a statistical indicator. It does not prove that any contract was broken up or that anyone acted improperly; it may reflect market prices, fixed budgets or separate needs.\nWhat can be checked: in the linked contract files, what was bought in each case and on which dates, and whether several contracts meet a single need that could have been procured at once.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"plantilla","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["k3D2hBs2yFRrSd8H4b2soA%3D%3D","4xvxr8TxIwbs%2BnLj3vAg5A%3D%3D","pgre5dAIjJc7u6%2B%2FR7DUoA%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}